.\"
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt ZFS-GUID 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm zfs-guid
.Nd ZFS GUI privileged backend service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl p Ar pidfile
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the privileged backend of the
.Xr zfs-gui 1
graphical manager.  It runs as
.Sq root
and executes only operations registered in a built-in whitelist,
using
.Xr execv 3
with an argument vector; no shell is ever invoked.
.Pp
The frontend connects through a
.Ux
domain socket, normally
.Pa /var/run/zfs-gui/zfs-gui.sock .
Peer credentials are obtained with
.Xr getpeereid 2
and checked against the configured user and group lists.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to standard error.  Useful for debugging.
.It Fl c Ar config
Read configuration from
.Ar config .
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/etc/zfs-gui.conf .
.It Fl p Ar pidfile
Write the process ID to
.Ar pidfile .
The default is
.Pa /var/run/zfs-gui.pid .
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses
.Ql key = value
lines; lines starting with
.Ql #
are comments.
.Bl -tag -width allowed_groups
.It Cm allowed_users
Comma-separated list of user names allowed to connect.
Root is always allowed.
.It Cm allowed_groups
Comma-separated list of group names allowed to connect.
The default is
.Ql wheel .
.It Cm socket_path
Path of the
.Ux
socket.
.It Cm socket_group
Group that owns the socket file.
.It Cm socket_mode
Octal permissions of the socket file.
The default is
.Ql 0660 .
.It Cm io_timeout
Timeout in seconds for ordinary operations; zero disables the limit.
.It Cm auth_mode
Password policy for dangerous operations:
.Ql dangerous
(the default; only destructive operations require a password),
.Ql all
(every state-changing operation requires a password), or
.Ql none
(never ask; not recommended).
.It Cm auth_max_attempts
Number of consecutive failed authentications before the user is locked out.
The default is 3.
.It Cm auth_lockout
Lockout duration in seconds.
The default is 300.
.El
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Destructive operations additionally require the calling user to re-enter an
administrator password, which is verified through
.Xr pam 3
using the
.Ql zfs-gui
service (falling back to
.Ql system ) .
The authenticated account must also be an administrator (root, or a member of
.Cm allowed_groups ) .
Passwords are never logged and are wiped from memory after use.
Failed attempts are rate limited per user ID.
.Pp
The daemon grants its clients the ability to run privileged ZFS
operations.  Restrict
.Cm allowed_groups
to administrators, and keep
.Cm socket_group
in sync so that the socket file itself is not reachable by
unprivileged users.
.Pp
Because every request is validated against the built-in operation table,
unknown operations, unknown flags, unknown options, and positional
arguments beginning with
.Ql -
are rejected.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/zfs-gui.conf -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/zfs-gui.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/zfs-gui
PAM service used for password re-authentication.
.It Pa /var/run/zfs-gui/zfs-gui.sock
Default socket path.
.It Pa /var/run/zfs-gui.pid
Default PID file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enable and start the service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysrc zfsguid_enable=YES
service zfsguid start
.Ed
.Pp
Run in the foreground for debugging:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zfs-guid -f -c /usr/local/etc/zfs-gui.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8 ,
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr getpeereid 2 ,
.Xr execv 3
.Sh AUTHORS
ZFS-GUI project.
